<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Specialty profits slip, plans new stores.</title>
<headline>Specialty profits slip, plans new stores.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>13 months ended March 31 vs pro-forma previous 13 months</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		16.3	  vs  20.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.7	   vs  5.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   35.08	 vs  41.61</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   48.22	 vs  61.72</p>
<p>    Tax			 13.14	 vs  20.11</p>
<p>    Finance costs	   7.57	  vs  7.51</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,372.73    vs  1,106.29</p>
<p>Div payable</p>
<p>on register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: Specialty Stores Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was offering capitalisation shares to ordinary and 'N' ordinary shareholders. Shareholders can elect to receive a cash dividend instead.</p>
<p>Specialty said that trading conditions would remain challenging particularly in the first half of the financial year as there was little indication of a short-term upturn in consumer spending.</p>
<p>It said its objective remained to establish a positive growth pattern again. This, it said, would be assisted by the launch of 79 new stores.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
